-- IELTS 5.5: second final test

B. The scheme began because traffic outside the school gates was heavy every morning. After one term, the number of cars stopping at the gates fell, and teachers reported that fewer children arrived late.

C. Volunteers wear bright jackets and carry a list of the children expected at each stop. The route avoids main roads where possible. If it rains heavily, the walking bus still runs, but parents may choose to drive instead.

D. The organisers now want to start a second route, but they say this will depend on finding more adult volunteers.', 'VALID');
